  "content": [
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 1,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "who walk -- The statement ends with \"Christ Jesus\"; the last ten words are interpolated."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 2,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Spirit -- Hitherto in Romans the Holy Spirit has been mentioned but once Romans 5:5 in this chapter He is mentioned nineteen times. Redemption is by blood and by power. (See Scofield \"Exodus 14:30\").; Romans 3:21-5:11; speaks of the redemptive price; Ro 8. of redemptive power.\n\nsin -- Sin. (See Scofield \"Romans 5:21\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 3,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "sin -- Sin. (See Scofield \"Romans 5:21\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 10,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "sin -- Sin. (See Scofield \"Romans 5:21\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 13,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "mortify -- make to die the doings of the body."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 16,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "children -- (Greek - τέκνον, \"one born,\" a child (and so in Romans 8:17,21); not, as in Romans 8:14, \"sons\" (gr. huios). See Galatians 4:1,7 where babyhood and sonhood are contrasted. Also \"Adoption\"; Romans 8:15,23; Ephesians 1:5."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 23,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "adoption -- Lit. placing as sons. See Adoption, Romans 8:15."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 38,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "angels -- (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\")."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 39,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "creature -- Or, created thing."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
